# No Xcode Builds in Cursor

- **Never** run `xcodebuild`, `./open-xcode.command` for build verification, or any other Xcode build/compile command from Cursor agents.
- Do not launch simulator builds to verify compilation unless the user explicitly asks to run a build.
- For Swift/iOS compile issues, fix from compiler errors shown in Xcode, linter diagnostics, or static code review — do not attempt to build in the terminal.
- If verification is needed, tell the user to build in Xcode locally.
